{"id": "EUVD-2026-86104", "enisaUuid": "9eddd0cb-29a2-3621-ae09-dad7773ac2d2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: ixp4xx - fix buffer chain unwind on allocation failure\n\nchainup_buffers() builds a linked list of buffer descriptors for a\nscatterlist. If dma_pool_alloc() fails while constructing the list, the\ncurrent code sets buf to NULL and later dereferences it unconditionally\nat the end of the function:\n\n  buf->next = NULL;\n  buf->phys_next = 0;\n\nThis can lead to a null-pointer dereference on allocation failure.\n\nIf the failure happens after part of the descriptor chain has already\nbeen allocated and DMA-mapped, the partially constructed chain also\nneeds to be released.\n\nFix this by terminating the partially constructed chain on allocation\nfailure and letting the callers unwind it via their existing cleanup\npaths. Also fix ablk_perform() to preserve the hook pointers before\nchecking for failure, so partially built chains can be freed correctly.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:04:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:59:03", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d4007867be42d71795b78fa7f8ce7514dda9ca83", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4918b0bd7d2baafb45d87dca9e322137c96005c2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8c37bc8d6a6f77bf9593fb1bcab6c14c7cf02991", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04cb00106ca4d0fa9eca24cadc4eda6036e855c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/028a7f4f3d69e551f6bf9f728d547bbf4cfc707d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/25056329384010a8672552b134f609601dc4f80e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mh76-mg38-r432", "CVE-2026-97506"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05a11cc3-ce41-3187-91e8-85c4b0c90188", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0d44dc59b2b434b29aafeae581d06f81efac7c83 <028a7f4f3d69e551f6bf9f728d547bbf4cfc707d"}, {"id": "0d3a2b9f-6b64-323b-a63c-60231c7daf22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0d44dc59b2b434b29aafeae581d06f81efac7c83 <25056329384010a8672552b134f609601dc4f80e"}, {"id": "18731f08-0e4c-3e0d-8fbc-d3139d846776", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0d44dc59b2b434b29aafeae581d06f81efac7c83 <04cb00106ca4d0fa9eca24cadc4eda6036e855c8"}, {"id": "242b80c4-d750-35a6-8ee2-311bb507877c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.30"}, {"id": "274415fa-91ab-3e64-9f11-4b6dbdc1005d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "481cff38-6680-3955-a962-f49c72ea2b83", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "4ce91e01-85f2-38c8-946d-fbb441e1f2ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.29.3 <2.6.30"}, {"id": "55f00ea5-8d9e-3767-bbbd-d25ba4018a80", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82a8becb9c2c52fc5e67057a43aeded1f0731e7b"}, {"id": "595839ba-3f16-3549-aea5-7ac3852b1d95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a80273150a8a1725fa70418d106eb1f2ee8fd2f"}, {"id": "5e233ca5-6379-3a62-aa03-5039b029c6b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.28.10 <2.6.29"}, {"id": "835b596a-19e5-3868-a049-b0a80488f735", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.27.22 <2.6.28"}, {"id": "915dd866-c97a-3818-81cc-3311437af3db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "68845515c8b11791b547a2838e22c27dfa3115ee"}, {"id": "94118c2d-2d7f-3546-be14-a1b388f55218", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "9e99b280-979e-3a92-bdfb-9bef886191c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "p